    {
      "content": "Before assuming a plan's 'preserve the -hard variants' Non-Goal is achievable, grep the whole repo for the literal -hard names first. In this codebase a prior, unrelated task can delete a component's -hard variants without the deleting task's own plan documenting that fact anywhere discoverable except via a fresh repo-wide grep -- trusting a plan's premise here silently produces false 'preserve X' instructions for an X that no longer exists.",
      "category": "INSIGHT",
      "source_artifact": "specs/125_delete_base_lifecycle_skills/summaries/01_delete-base-lifecycle-skills-summary.md",
