        "stale-premise"
      ]
    },
    {
      "content": "git-commit-scoped.sh's V2 safety gate drops a pathspec when neither `[ -e \"$p\" ]` nor `git ls-files --error-unmatch -- \"$p\"` succeeds. A file staged for deletion via `git rm` fails BOTH checks (removed from the index by git rm, and no longer on disk), so passing the exact deleted file's path as a pathspec silently drops it from the commit with only a WARN, and the commit succeeds without it -- easy to miss. Workaround: pass the still-existing PARENT DIRECTORY as the pathspec instead (e.g. the skills/ directory containing sibling skills), which passes the `[ -e \"$p\" ]` check and correctly includes the staged deletion.",
      "category": "TECHNIQUE",
